  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most Cameroonians carry a French or English Christian first name (Serge, Christelle, Emmanuel, Blessing) or a Muslim one in the north, and a family name that is often a native name from the father or grandfather. On forms and in school lists the family name comes first, so people are often called 'Kamga Serge' or 'Mbarga Christelle'. The names tell where a family comes from: Fotso and Kamdem are Bamiléké, Mbarga and Atangana are Beti, Ekwalla and Ebongue are Duala, Che and Ngwa are from the North-West, Lyonga and Ayuk from the South-West. Many men add Junior or Fils when named after their father.",
